m text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Add a free paycheck, mortgage, or tax refund calculator to your firm website. White-labeled, mobile-responsive, and entirely client-side — your clients’ data never touches your servers or ours.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"All 50 State Tax Profiles\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Each state has its own calculator with current 2026 brackets, standard deductions, and personal exemptions — sourced from each state’s Department of Revenue. Perfect for multi-state return preparation and client relocations.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"2026 OBBBA Comparison Tool\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"The OBBBA tax calculator compares your clients’ 2026 federal income tax under the new One Big Beautiful Bill Act against what they would have paid if the TCJA had sunset. Includes the $40,400 SALT cap, $2,200 CTC, and tip/overtime deductions.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h3\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Full Published Methodology\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Every formula, source, and assumption is documented on our methodology page. Cite us in client memos, share the link with skeptical clients, or use our data tables in your own research. All sources are official IRS, SSA, and state revenue department publications.\\\"}]]}]]}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1a:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-10 rounded-xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-emerald-500/5 p-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Why Tax Professionals Use TheTaxCalc\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Professional preparers tell us they use TheTaxCalc for three reasons. First, our calculators load instantly and work without an account — perfect for showing a client the impact of a salary increase or a relocation mid-meeting. Second, our data is current and fully sourced. We update federal figures within 48 hours of any IRS publication, and our state data is sourced directly from each state’s revenue department. Third, because all calculations run client-side, there are no data privacy concerns about client income passing through a third-party server.\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Many firms also use our free embeddable widgets to add interactive calculators to their own websites without paying for a vendor solution. The widgets can be styled to match your firm’s brand, and there is no per-visitor fee or usage cap. If you need a calculator type we don’t currently offer, we accept requests and often build requested tools within a few weeks.\\\"}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-10\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Most-Used Calculators for Professionals\